			  Software reconfiguration required. </description>
              <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RB_EP_RX_TOUT_MODE</name>
              <description>This bit is 1, and when the continuous burst packet is received, PP=1 and not a short packet,
			  the DPH is not received after the timeout, resulting in TOUT_IF interrupt.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
			<field>
              <name>RB_EP_RX_FIFO_CFG</name>
              <description>The object being operated on when the access offset address is 0xC~0xF</description>
              <bitOffset>5</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
			<field>
              <name>RB_EP_RX_FIFO_MODE</name>
              <description>A bit of 1 indicates that the current endpoint is using the FIFO mode, 
			  and the start and end addresses of the FIFO should be configured before the bit is 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>6</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
			<field>
              <name>RB_EP_RX_CHAIN_AUTO</name>
              <description>CHAIN automatically switches mode, this mode is recommended.</description>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>			
		 </fields>
